# Public run-report format

`reports/public/public-20260906-063336.md` is the reference. Every newer run report
(`public-<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>.md`) must reproduce this H2 skeleton **in this order**.
Counts inside headings are run-specific — keep the shape, change the numbers.

1. `## Config`
2. `## Result summary (classification-aware)` — incl. `### ✅ Manual audit is the ground truth (headline numbers)` and the `### Metrics (manual audit = ground truth)` comparison
3. `## Manual audit verdicts (<N>, evidence-based)` — one `### Day <n> — X PASS / Y FAIL / Z HALLUCINATION` per day
4. `## Totals (manual audit)`
5. `## Interaction (ASK USER) — SINGLE (<n> tasks)`
6. `## Interaction (ASK USER) — MULTI (<n> tasks) + KBIQ`
7. `## Hallucination controls (<n> tasks) — standalone` — incl. `### DeepEval vs manual audit (HC setup check)` and `### DeepEval HC judge compute stats (this run only)`
8. `## Failure analysis (<n> FAIL)`
9. `## Device telemetry & cost`
10. `## Sensitive-info scan (privacy habit)`
11. `## Audit methodology & on-device verification` — incl. `### Limitations`
12. `## Artifacts`

## A missing section means "go find the data", not "drop the heading"

Fill it from the run's own artifacts:

- Verdicts / totals / failure analysis → `assets/runs/public/<run>/day*/` (`meta.json`, `output.json`, `trajectory.json`, `ui_states/`) and `benchmarks/androidlife-530/` (`public.md`, `ask_user_facts_public.json`, `multiturn_kb_public.json`, `hallucination_controls.json`)
- KBIQ → the run's `kb_audit.json`
- Telemetry → `run_metrics.json`, `samples.ndjson` (1 Hz battery/thermal), `llm_proxy_metrics.jsonl` (per-request tokens)
- HC → `reports/metrics/hallucination/<run>.{json,md}`
- Official scores → `reports/metrics/public/<run>-report.{json,md}`

If the artifacts are not local, mirror the non-image files from
[YuvrajSingh9886/androidlife-public](https://huggingface.co/datasets/YuvrajSingh9886/androidlife-public)
under `runs/<run>/` first. GIFs and screenshots are not required.

## Rules

- Manual audit is the ground truth: the headline number is the manual verdict, never the official self-reported one. Show both.
- The telemetry table must carry every `063336` row: agent LLM cost + request count, `ask_user` cost + calls, grand total, agent tokens (prompt/completion/total), battery Δ-pct sum, `app_battery` mAh total, max CPU/GPU/NPU temp, max power-amp/skin temp, max battery/vendor-phone temp, thermal status, wall-clock.
- **No extra H2/H3 headings.** The skeleton above is the whole outline. Extra content that
  used to get its own section (a re-run record, an official-vs-manual discrepancy table, a
  false-pass callout table, seed/leftover findings, death/resume notes) must be folded into the
  relevant canonical section as prose, a bold label paragraph, a blockquote or a table. A
  **missing** canonical section is not allowed either.
  - re-run records / superseded verdicts → end of `## Totals (manual audit)`
  - official-vs-manual discrepancies → the `### Metrics` blockquote (they are usually already there)
  - false-pass / classification callouts → end of `## Failure analysis`
  - seed, leftover-state, death/resume findings → `## Audit methodology & on-device verification`
- Keep the `### Day <n> — X PASS / Y FAIL / Z HALLUCINATION (…)` heading shape; run-specific
  counts and suffixes go in the parentheses, never in a new heading.
- Any verdict superseded by a re-run must say so inline, with the date.
- Verify before shipping: `grep -n '^#\{2,3\} ' reports/public/<report>.md` — the output must
  match the 12-H2 skeleton above with no additions.
